<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45323" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτρά̆πελ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέπω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easily turning</i> or <i>changing</i>, of the
			Athenians, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				5.13
			</span></i>; <i>nimble</i>, of apes, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>NA</u>
				5.26
			</span></i>; in earlier Gr. always metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος
				εὐ</span>. <i>a dexterous, ready</i> plea, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				469
			</span></i> (lyr.). Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λως</span>
			<i>dexterously, readily, without awkwardness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>ready with an answer</i> or <i>repartee, witty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1108a24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1128a10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. παρὰ τὰς συνουσίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					23.5.7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίτθη εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.227a
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				9.23.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> in bad sense,
				<i>jesting, ribald</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				7.49
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτράπελόν ἐστι</span> c. acc.
			et inf., it is <i>ludicrous</i> that . . , <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1062b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>tricky, dishonest</i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.105
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. κέρδη</span>
			<i>time-serving</i> arts, of flatterers, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.92
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
